  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte and Touche has $461M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The firm won 156 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $3M. Obligations fell 31.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $193M so far this fiscal year. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $95.3M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $37M. Deloitte and Touche’s work is concentrated in a few markets: Other Computer Related Services accounts for $357M, Other Accounting Services accounts for $74.3M, and Offices of Certified Public Accountants accounts for $15.4M. Custom Computer Programming Services and several other professional services markets also appear in the top markets list. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the figures shown are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values in award tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Deloitte and Touche’s FY2026 obligations compare to prior years?",
        "body": "Deloitte and Touche obligated $461M in FY2026 to date, which is lower than several prior fiscal years. The firm obligated $734M in FY23, $701M in FY24, and $669M in FY25. Obligations were $567M in FY22 and $384M in FY21."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies provide the most work to Deloitte and Touche in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $193M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $95.3M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $37M. The Department of the Treasury, Social Security Administration, and Department of Veterans Affairs follow with $30.8M, $25.5M, and $24.5M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
